    Question(
      id: "sci_ch5_ex_q01",
      subject: Subject.science,
      chapterId: "sci_ch_05_life_processes",
      questionText: "[NCERT Exercise 1] Which of the following statements is NOT a correct statement about the trends when going from left to right across the periods of the Periodic Table?",
      options: const [
        QuestionOption(id: "A", text: "The atoms lose their electrons more easily.", isCorrect: true),
        QuestionOption(id: "B", text: "The elements become less metallic in nature.", isCorrect: false),
        QuestionOption(id: "C", text: "The number of valence electrons increases.", isCorrect: false),
        QuestionOption(id: "D", text: "The oxides become more acidic.", isCorrect: false),
      ],
      stepByStepSolution: "Correct Answer: (A) The atoms lose their electrons more easily.\n\nScientific Principle / Key Concept:\nMoving from left to right across a period:\n1. Valence electrons increase from 1 to 8.\n2. Effective nuclear charge increases as protons are added to the nucleus while electrons enter the same shell.\n3. Atomic radius decreases, holding valence electrons more tightly.\n4. Therefore, ionization enthalpy increases, meaning atoms lose electrons with greater difficulty (less easily).\n5. Consequently, metallic character decreases and oxides become more acidic.\nThus, statement (c) / option (A) is INCORRECT.\n\nDetailed Distractor & Misconception Analysis:\n• Option (B): True statement (metallic character decreases).\n• Option (C): True statement (valence electrons increase from 1 to 8).\n• Option (D): True statement (oxides transition from basic to acidic).",
      difficultyLevel: DifficultyLevel.medium,
      status: QuestionStatus.approved,
      submittedBy: '00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001',
      reviewedBy: '00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001',
      createdAt: DateTime.fromMillisecondsSinceEpoch(1727200000000 + 16000),
    ),
