      stepByStepSolution: "Correct Answer: (A) Magnesium (\$\\text{Mg}\$)\n\nScientific Principle / Key Concept:\n• The chemical formula \$\\text{XCl}_2\$ shows that element X has a combining capacity (valency) of 2.\n• A solid with a high melting point indicates an ionic compound.\n• Among the given options:\n  - \$\\text{Na}\$ (Group 1): Valency = 1 \$\\rightarrow \\text{NaCl}\$\n  - \$\\text{Mg}\$ (Group 2): Valency = 2 \$\\rightarrow \\text{MgCl}_2\$ (ionic solid, high MP)\n  - \$\\text{Al}\$ (Group 13): Valency = 3 \$\\rightarrow \\text{AlCl}_3\$\n  - \$\\text{Si}\$ (Group 14): Valency = 4 \$\\rightarrow \\text{SiCl}_4\$\nTherefore, X belongs to Group 2, the same group as Magnesium (\$\\text{Mg}\$).\n\nDetailed Distractor & Misconception Analysis:\n• Option (B): Na forms \$\\text{NaCl}\$.\n• Option (C): Al forms \$\\text{AlCl}_3\$.\n• Option (D): Si forms \$\\text{SiCl}_4\$.",
      difficultyLevel: DifficultyLevel.easy,
      status: QuestionStatus.approved,
      submittedBy: '00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001',
      reviewedBy: '00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001',
      createdAt: DateTime.fromMillisecondsSinceEpoch(1727200000000 + 17000),
    ),
