      stepByStepSolution: "Correct Answer: (A) Neon (\$\\text{Ne}\$, \$Z=10\$), with electronic configuration \$2, 8\$\n\nScientific Principle / Key Concept:\n• The maximum capacity of K shell (\$n=1\$) is \$2(1)^2 = 2\$ electrons.\n• The maximum capacity of L shell (\$n=2\$) is \$2(2)^2 = 8\$ electrons.\n• An element with both shells completely filled has electronic configuration \$2, 8\$.\n• Total electrons = \$2 + 8 = 10\$, which corresponds to Neon (\$\\text{Ne}\$).\n\nDetailed Distractor & Misconception Analysis:\n• Option (B): Ar has 3 shells (\$2, 8, 8\$).\n• Option (C): He has only 1 shell (\$2\$).\n• Option (D): F has \$2, 7\$ (unfilled second shell).",
