      stepByStepSolution: "Correct Answer: (A) Mendeléev's Table is based on increasing atomic masses with 8 groups (divided into sub-groups A and B), could not position isotopes, and had anomalous inverted mass pairs; the Modern Periodic Table is based on increasing atomic numbers with 18 distinct vertical groups and 7 horizontal periods, naturally accommodating isotopes and resolving all mass inversions.\n\nScientific Principle / Key Concept:\nComparison:\n1. Basis of Classification:\n• Mendeléev's Table: Atomic mass (Properties are periodic function of atomic masses).\n• Modern Periodic Table: Atomic number (Properties are periodic function of atomic numbers).\n2. Structure:\n• Mendeléev: 8 Groups (subdivided into A and B sub-groups) and 6 Periods.\n• Modern Table: 18 Vertical columns (Groups) and 7 Horizontal rows (Periods).\n3. Anomalies & Isotopes:\n• Mendeléev could not assign a fixed place to hydrogen or isotopes, and had anomalous pairs (Co before Ni, Te before I).\n• Modern Table places isotopes in the same position and puts Co (\$Z=27\$) before Ni (\$Z=28\$) without anomaly.\n\nDetailed Distractor & Misconception Analysis:\n• Option (B): Inverts the historical basis.\n• Option (C): Noble gases are in Group 18, never Group 1.\n• Option (D): Confuses Newlands with Mendeléev.",
